{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7Kr6Nkc6eWwVjrTt4am","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's the summary, at about 270 words.\n\n<final_document>\n**Project Summary: Tenant Defense Project**\n\nLast year, 1,140 eviction cases were filed in [County]. The Tenant Defense Project represented the tenant in 163 of them. We turned away about 300 more tenants because no attorney was available. Each of our two attorneys carries about 80 open cases.\n\nIn June, one of those two attorneys is leaving. Unless we hire, we will drop to one attorney and be able to represent about half as many tenants. We request $90,000 over two years ($45,000 per year) toward a full-time staff attorney so that tenants facing eviction in [County] can still get a lawyer.\n\n**Outcomes.** In cases where we represented the tenant, 58% ended with the tenant staying in the home or getting at least 60 days to move. We do not yet have a comparable figure for tenants without a lawyer in our county. Starting in January, we will request court-wide outcome data from the county clerk so we can measure the difference representation makes.\n\n**Plan.** The departing attorney has agreed to spend her last month training the new hire. Based on current caseloads, the new attorney will carry about 80 cases. Every six months we will report to the Foundation on cases opened and how they ended.\n\n**Budget.** The position costs $78,000 per year with benefits. Of that, the Foundation's award would cover $45,000, a family fund has pledged $20,000 per year for both years, and the remaining $13,000 comes from our general budget. Our general budget includes a $60,000 county contract that is up for renewal in October.\n\nMaria Chen, Managing Attorney\n</final_document>\n\nSome decisions you should check before you submit:\n\n- **I called it a \"staff attorney,\" not a \"third attorney.\"** Without a separate plan for the June vacancy, this hire takes you back to two attorneys, not up to three. A reviewer who reads \"third attorney\" next to \"one is leaving in June\" will notice the mismatch. The framing I used, keeping the clinic from dropping to one lawyer, is accurate and still makes a strong case. If you do find another way to fill the vacancy, change it back.\n- **I included the county contract renewal.** It's the funding risk the reviewers are most likely to learn about anyway, and it reads better coming from you. You can cut that sentence if you'd prefer to cover it only in the budget narrative.\n- **I left out sustainability after two years** because you don't have a plan yet. The full application will probably ask about it, so it's worth thinking about before March 3.\n- **The timing is tight.** The foundation decides in May, the attorney leaves in June, and your last hire took five months. The training month may not overlap with the new hire's start. I kept the sentence about training because it's true, but I didn't promise a start date.\n- **Replace [County]** with your county's name."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":10184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1099},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"984e0169-2df1-471d-9fb3-2896fdd296a5","uuid":"cdd4bd43-80b8-44a4-bc59-108ffa9077eb","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:35:30.582Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7Kr69rqguBodCKUrzvY"}
